meta {
  name: List Location Filter Options
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/public/colleges/locations/filter-options
  body: none
  auth: none
}

query {
  ~state: Kerala
  ~streamId:
  ~disciplineId:
  ~studyLevelId:
  ~programTypeId:
  ~courseMasterId:
  ~courseName:
  ~universityId:
}

docs {
  State options for the explore filter flow's "choose a state" step, or
  district options inside one state. No auth.

  Query (all optional):
  - state — when sent, returns districts in that state instead of states
    (case-insensitive)
  - streamId (ignored if disciplineId is set), disciplineId, studyLevelId,
    programTypeId, courseMasterId / courseName, universityId — the choices
    already made, same meaning as List Colleges

  Response without `state`:
  data: [{ state: string, collegeCount: number }]

  Response with `state`:
  data: [{ district: string, collegeCount: number }]

  Sorted by collegeCount desc, then name. Not paginated.

  - Only active, publicly listed colleges that match the other filters.
  - State names use the official spelling (same list as GET /public/india-states).
    Colleges with no state or an unrecognised state are left out.
  - Colleges without a district are counted in the state but have no
    district option, so district counts can add up to less than the state's.
  - Every option returns exactly `collegeCount` colleges when passed to
    List Colleges as `state` (and `district`) with the same filters.
}
